    "value": "0"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2003-p24.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Expand: \\[ \\begin{aligned} &\\log_a\\dfrac ab+\\log_b\\dfrac ba \\\\ &\\quad {}=(1-\\log_a b)+(1-\\log_b a) \\\\ &\\quad {}=2-\\left(\\log_a b+\\log_b a\\right). \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nLet \\(c=\\log_a b\\gt0.\\) Since \\(c+\\dfrac1c\\ge2\\) by AM-GM, the expression is at most \\(0.\\)\n\nEquality holds when \\(c=1,\\) that is, when \\(a=b,\\) so the largest value is \\(0.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Simplify to \\(2-\\log_a b-\\log_b a\\)",
        "With \\(c=\\log_a b\\gt0,\\) use \\(c+\\dfrac1c\\ge2\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
